Paolo Francese (francese@polito.it) wrote:
: When I try to mount a NFS file system I get the following error:
:    Can't get net id for host
: 
: Can anyone explain me what does it mean?

Post your "mount" command.  Note the remote host's name on the command line.  

Now, given that host's name, can you convert that to an IP address, either by
looking it up in the /etc/hosts file, or by the "nslookup" command?  If not,
that's your error: NFS can't get the net-id for host.

        Stu



