>Desktop Environment mail tool (dtmail) and in Netscape Messenger.  However,
>Pine seems to be much fussier about recognizing these folders.  Most of the
>folders are handled just fine in Pine, but a significant number of them are
>not recognized by Pine.  Does anybody know why this is, and what can be done
>about it?

Upon further examination, it appears that Pine is complaining about the
formatting of the date in the "From" line.  When the mailcv program produces
"From" lines like

	From xxx@xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx Thu Nov 19 16:13:38 1998

then Pine is happy.  However, sometimes it produces "From" lines like

	From xxx@xxx.xxx.xxx.xxxMon, 01 Jan 1976 09:00:00 -000 

or even completely messed up, like

	From xxx@xxx.xxx.xxx Mon 06  eb 8:51 190:

I've also noticed that messages received after the first of the year end up
with "From" lines like

	From xxx@xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx Tue Feb  1 0 1920

which are also rejected by Pine.  I've finally been bitten by the Y2K bug!

Oh, well,

William Thompson



